1. Words used here

"the Software" is Etiuda: every version of the software published in the
repository this file sits in, in source form and in any build made from that
source.

"the Licensor" is Maxim Gwiazda.

"you" is the person or the organisation exercising the rights below.

"production use" is using the Software to do real work: real conversations,
real customers, real business of any kind. Reading the source, studying it,
trying it out, demonstrating it, and developing or testing changes to it are
not production use.

"personal purposes" is your own use, for yourself or your household: study,
hobby, and your own projects. It is not personal if you are doing your job,
paid or unpaid, or if the use is in or for a business.

A catalog is not part of the Software. A catalog file holds somebody's own
content, it carries its own terms, and this licence says nothing about it.


